      "description": "Expression of Interest – School of Psychological Sciences Casual Tutors - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Expression of Interest – School of Psychological Sciences Casual Tutors 504399 Burnie, TAS Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Casual Closing on: 12 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Access flexible casual teaching opportunities that align with your availability and expertise Join a supportive team and help develop the next generation of your profession Available across multiple University locations – Burnie, Hobart and Launceston About the Role As a casual academic you will support teaching within the Bachelor of Psychological Sciences and related postgraduate programs. Typical responsibilities include delivering tutorials and workshops.. Depending on requirements, responsibilities may also include student support, marking, invigilation, and providing assistance in developing teaching materials. How to Register: To express your interest, please submit the following as part of your application: Cover letter (1 page) outlining your motivation for joining this role Resume Copies of relevant qualifications and certifications Any preferred locations and availability Expressions of Interest will be assessed on receipt. You will be contacted if opportunities matching your skills and experience become available. Please note: Your application does not guarantee casual opportunities. Eligibility: Applicants must have: A four-year or equivalent tertiary qualification in a relevant field and/or equivalent qualifications and/or professional experience. A demonstrated understanding of psychological science concepts and methods. Academic, clinical, and/or professional experience relevant to the position. High level communication skills with a demonstrated ability to build rapport with a diverse range of organisations and people, and to work collaboratively and harmoniously as a valued member of a team Desirable: Experience in University-level education within the field of expertise. Tasmanian Working With Vulnerable People Registration Position Description - 504399 - School of Psychological Sciences Casual EOI.pdf Enquiries: For further information about this Expression of Interest, please contact: ppsw.pda@utas.edu.au Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 2eb8d3cc Last Name (required) aac9728e Email (required) bff637c2 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related