    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/learning-adviser-stem-numeracy-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy)",
      "description": "Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) 504349 Hobart, TAS Part time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Provide tailored support to students through consultations, workshops, webinars and learning resources Identify and respond to emerging student learning needs and challenges. Part-time (0.4 FTE) ongoing role based in Hobart The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The Learning Adviser (STEM and Numeracy) provides specialist learning development support to students studying in disciplines that require scientific literacy, numeracy, quantitative reasoning, mathematics, statistics, data interpretation and other STEM-related capabilities. Working collaboratively with academic and College staff, the role identifies emerging student needs, learning trends and study challenges to ensure support services remain relevant, responsive and effective. The Learning Adviser also contributes to the delivery and success of peer learning programs as required. Through individual consultations, the Learning Adviser supports students with diverse learning needs while contributing to the continuous improvement of learning services, resources and programs. This includes developing and enhancing online and face-to-face initiatives such as UniStart, the Study Toolkit, workshops and webinars that foster independent learning and academic success. What you’ll do: Provide individual consultations to students seeking assistance with numeracy, quantitative reasoning, mathematics, statistics, scientific literacy and related academic learning skills. Contribute to the review, development, and promotion of a range of learning services, resources, and programs to support student learning. Collaborate with key stakeholders to support student development of scientific literacy, numeracy, and other STEM-related academic skills within the context of courses and units. Work collaboratively with Student Support Services and key stakeholders to understand the learning needs of students. Work within a culture of continuous improvement, taking a solution-focused approach to identifying issues and recommending improvements in consultation with the Manager. What we’re looking for: A degree in Education, Mathematics, Statistics, Science, Engineering, Health Sciences or another relevant discipline Experience teaching or supporting students in a range of learning environments, including one-on-one, small and large classes, and both online and face-to-face settings. Demonstrated experience in providing STEM learning support, including numeracy development, quantitative reasoning, mathematics, statistics, and scientific literacy. Understanding of the needs of students from diverse educational, cultural and linguistic backgrounds, including neurodiverse learners and students returning to study. Successful experience in the planning, development, delivery, monitoring and evaluation of learning services and programs. Excellent organisational and management skills, including the ability to use initiative, prioritise, solve problems, and meet deadlines Demonstrated ability to work effectively both independently and collaboratively, with strong communication and interpersonal skills, and a commitment to innovative, student-centred practice that responds to diverse learning needs and evolving educational environments. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 7 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $130,943 (pro rata) comprising base salary within the range of $101,821 to $111,917 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Dr I-Lien Tsay, Manager, Learning and Academic Skills at ILien.Tsay@utas.edu.au or 03 62264784. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description below for full details. Position Description - 504349 - Learning Advisor (STEM and Numeracy).pdf Applications close Sunday, 25 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) af9afe26 Last Name (required) 0eee6813 Email (required) 533f7d29 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer Sydney, NSW. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS. Melbourne, VIC Teaching Intensive Shape the future of advanced nursing practice through leadership in Nurse education, research and national healthcare collaboration. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert e5e8aeb2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Services Teaching Support Student Services Teaching Support Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) b2452045 Last Name (required) 077f6853 Email (required) a01eedda Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
