    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-english-hobart-tas-australia-launceston": {
      "title": "Lecturer in English",
      "description": "Lecturer in English - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer in English 504310 Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 26 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Deliver engaging and high-quality teaching across the English and Writing major, with a particular focus on literary studies, in face-to-face, blended and online learning environments Enjoy generous superannuation, flexible work arrangements, professional development opportunities and health and wellbeing benefits Full-time,  fixed-term two year role (2027/2028), based in either Launceston or Hobart About the opportunity The School of Humanities & Social Sciences is seeking a Lecturer in English to deliver high-quality teaching and learning experiences in English, with a particular focus on literary studies. We welcome applications from scholars who can teach across the breadth of the English and Writing major and who are passionate about fostering critical thinking, creativity and cultural understanding. As a teaching-intensive academic, you will design, coordinate and deliver contemporary, student-centred learning experiences across face-to-face, blended and fully online environments. Working collaboratively within a supportive academic team, you will contribute to curriculum development, unit coordination, and a scholarly approach to teaching and learning, while also undertaking research aligned with your workload allocation. This role offers the opportunity to contribute to the University's place-based vision and strengthen connections between the discipline, the University and the wider community through public-facing Humanities initiatives. You will join a collaborative academic team committed to delivering an outstanding student experience and showcasing the value of Humanities in contemporary society. Accountabilities and Outcomes (What you’ll do): Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate English and Writing units, including face-to-face, blended and online learning. Coordinate and develop units, including curriculum design, implementation and continuous improvement. Create engaging, inclusive and academically rigorous learning experiences that support student success and progression. Contribute to innovative teaching practices, including contemporary and flexible approaches to learning and assessment. Maintain an active research and scholarly profile appropriate to a teaching-intensive Level B academic position. Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience (What we’re looking for): A PhD in literary studies or a closely related discipline. Demonstrated experience teaching literary studies at university level, including coordinating units and supporting student success. Proven ability to design, deliver and assess high-quality curriculum aligned with learning outcomes. Experience delivering engaging and inclusive learning experiences across face-to-face, blended and online environments. An emerging or established research and scholarly profile appropriate to career stage and a teaching-intensive Level B academic position. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Associate Professor Naomi Milthorpe, Naomi.Milthorpe@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Lecturer in English - Position Description - 504310.pdf Applications close Monday, 26 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) c6333b68 Last Name (required) 83d9a3a9 Email (required) 0ee06879 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer Sydney, NSW. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS. Melbourne, VIC Teaching Intensive Shape the future of advanced nursing practice through leadership in Nurse education, research and national healthcare collaboration. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 306d107b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 3f1b3ccd Last Name (required) de56527a Email (required) 78c021a2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
