    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/teaching-laboratory-technician-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Teaching Laboratory Technician",
      "description": "Teaching Laboratory Technician - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Teaching Laboratory Technician 504302 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 1 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Support hands-on teaching and practical learning within IMAS laboratory environments Enjoy a varied, hands-on role with great employee benefits, flexibility and 17% superannuation Full-time, fixed-term position until October 2027, based in Hobart About the opportunity The Teaching Laboratory Technician provides hands-on support for the delivery and overall management of laboratory practicals and related experiments. You will help ensure the effective and safe operation of teaching laboratory spaces, provide day-to-day technical and operational support, and assist with the planning and preparation of practical classes and training. During semester, some early starts and later finishes will be required to support the preparation and pack-up of practical classes. Working closely with the Laboratory Manager and Principal Laboratory Manager, you will be an integral member of the IMAS Operations team, supporting teaching activities across the Salamanca and Taroona facilities. What you’ll do: Help manage and organise the teaching laboratories across Salamanca and Taroona to accommodate a wide range of activities which will overlap from week to week and be ever changing. Communicate with the unit coordinators and demonstrators about their needs for each specific practical to provide technical support and lead the preparation. Set up and pack up equipment before and after laboratory practicals. Help with the running of teaching related experiments, such as culture of algae and shellfish, as well as limited field work. Assist with the making of custom equipment if required. Provide feedback to the Laboratory Manager regarding the safety of the practicals if required What we’re looking for: Completion of a Science Degree preferably marine. Significant experience in providing technical laboratory support of marine research infrastructure. Previous laboratory experience and working with students in a lab environment. Ability to work well with a range of people under different circumstances, in a professional yet friendly and approachable manner. Experience in working to firm timelines and demonstrated ability to adapt to changing requirements and priorities. Work, Health and Safety (WHS) knowledge and safe work systems management, including knowledge of chemical and laboratory hazards. Demonstrated ability to analyse and solve complex technical and non-technical problems and to adapt rapidly to changing priorities and tasks. Excellent oral, written, and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact effectively with a wide range of people and organisations and negotiate with senior representatives from internal and external organisations. High level organisational skills and a demonstrated capacity to act independently within established guidelines, using discretion and sound judgement. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Axel Durand, Laboratory Manager, axel.durand@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Teaching Laboratory Technician - Position Description - 504302.pdf Applications close Sunday, 1 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 3971e869 Last Name (required) c7b8e068 Email (required) 7077a910 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer Sydney, NSW. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS. Melbourne, VIC Teaching Intensive Shape the future of advanced nursing practice through leadership in Nurse education, research and national healthcare collaboration. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b79fb2b1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Laboratory & Research Support Laboratory & Research Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 5d2345f6 Last Name (required) 0e51683e Email (required) 5faf24a6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most 