    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/nurse-practitioner-senior-lecturer-sydney-nsw-australia-melbourne-vic-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas": {
      "title": "Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer",
      "description": "Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Sydney, NSW, Australia - Melbourne, VIC, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Nurse Practitioner Senior Lecturer 504366 Sydney, NSW Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Melbourne, VIC Part time Closing on: 26 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Lead the future of Nurse education in Australia Drive high-impact teaching, research and industry partnerships Ongoing 0.4 FTE opportunity with flexible remote work from anywhere in Australia, or on campus (Burnie, Hobart, Launceston or Sydney) About the Opportunity The University of Tasmania is seeking an endorsed Nurse Practitioner with a strong background in nursing education to join the School of Nursing as a Senior Lecturer. This is an exciting opportunity to provide academic leadership in the development and delivery of innovative Nurse Practitioner education, supporting the preparation of the next generation of advanced practice nurses across Australia. Working collaboratively with colleagues, industry partners and healthcare providers, you will contribute to the continued growth and excellence of the University's postgraduate Nurse Practitioner programs, while advancing research and scholarship that improves healthcare outcomes and strengthens the national Nurse Practitioner workforce. This ongoing position is offered at 0.4 FTE , providing flexibility to balance academic work alongside clinical practice and other professional commitments. What you’ll do Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University's strategic objectives and academic mission. Lead the development, delivery and ongoing enhancement of high-quality Nurse Practitioner curriculum at Master's level. Support students pursuing Nurse Practitioner endorsement pathways. Deliver engaging and evidence-based teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing programs. Build and maintain productive partnerships with healthcare providers, professional organisations and other stakeholders across Australia. Undertake and contribute to high-quality research, scholarship and knowledge translation activities. Foster a collaborative and inclusive academic culture focused on excellence in learning, teaching and research. What we’re looking for Endorsement as a Nurse Practitioner with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia (NMBA). Demonstrated experience in Nurse Practitioner education and curriculum development. A strong record of scholarly activity and a commitment to research that contributes to the nursing profession. Experience teaching and supporting student learning within higher education. Proven ability to build and maintain effective partnerships across healthcare, education and professional sectors. Current clinical expertise and professional currency relevant to advanced nursing practice. A PhD is preferred; applicants with a Master's qualification and significant relevant expertise are encouraged to apply. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. You’ll have access an array of staff benefits and discounts including. 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation (pro-rata). How to Apply? To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Annette Saunders, Interim Associate Head Learning and Teaching Postgraduate, annette.saunders@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position description will be inserted here Applications close Monday. 26th October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 12b4a5cd Last Name (required) fd8b61d8 Email (required) 9460853b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert a36ff467 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Melbourne, VIC, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Sydney, NSW, Australia Melbourne, VIC, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Sydney, NSW, Australia First Name (required) f7eafd5e Last Name (required) 870b72b8 Email (required) b3454468 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
