    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/learning-and-teaching-support-officer-hobart-tas-australia-launceston": {
      "title": "Learning and Teaching Support Officer",
      "description": "Learning and Teaching Support Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Learning and Teaching Support Officer 504334 Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Ensure the smooth delivery of all key learning and teaching operations Deliver high-quality customer service by responding to student and staff enquiries Full Time, Ongoing role based in Hobart or Launceston The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The Learning and Teaching Support Officer plays a key role in ensuring the effective delivery and support of learning and teaching activities across four Schools; School of Information and Communication Technology , School of Geography, Planning, and Spatial Sciences , School of Architecture and Design , and the School of Engineering . As our new Learning and Teaching Support Officer, you will provide high-quality administrative support for both onshore and offshore activities, including examinations, results processing, timetabling, resourcing, and workforce planning. This is a dynamic and varied role that requires strong administrative capability, sound judgement, excellent problem-solving skills, and a commitment to delivering exceptional service to staff and students. Our ideal candidate is highly organised, adaptable, and collaborative, with excellent communication and relationship-building skills. You will be capable of managing competing priorities, working independently when required, and contributing positively as part of a broader team. In this role, you will also contribute to continuous improvement initiatives, policy and process development, data analysis, reporting, strategic planning, and budget activities, helping to ensure the smooth and efficient operation of learning and teaching across the Schools. What you’ll do: Ensure the smooth delivery of all key learning and teaching operations, including exams, results, timetabling, and workforce planning. Provide accurate and timely administrative support to ensure compliance with University policies, procedures, and relevant regulatory requirements across learning and teaching activities, including Work Integrated Learning (WIL), transnational education (TNE), and other specialised programs. Deliver high-quality customer service by responding to student and staff enquiries, providing clear advice and support, and contributing to a positive learning and teaching experience. Support the continuous improvement of policies, processes, and operational practices, while contributing to strategic planning, data analysis, reporting, and budget management activities. Contribute to course and unit-related reporting and reviews, accreditation, and operational planning. Develop and maintain productive relationships with internal and external stakeholders, including academic staff, University leaders, industry partners, and government agencies, to support the successful delivery of programs and initiatives. ­ What we’re looking for: Demonstrated administrative experience in a complex organisation, with the ability to quickly develop an understanding of learning and teaching processes, including examinations, timetabling, results processing, and student progression. Proven ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and coordinate complex activities, including workforce planning and resource allocation, while maintaining a high level of accuracy and attention to detail. Experience in analysing data to support decision-making, budget control, and strategic planning, with the ability to identify insights and recommend improvements to enhance operational efficiency. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills, with the ability to build productive relationships, collaborate across diverse teams, engage with external stakeholders, and deliver high-quality service to staff and students. Demonstrated discretion, sound judgement and professionalism when handling sensitive and confidential matters involving students, staff, and stakeholders. Experience coordinating education programs or similar initiatives, including managing enrolments, supporting participants, coordinating inductions, and monitoring progress, is desirable. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Brendan Theodore, School Coordinator on Brendan.Theodore@utas.edu.au . Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504334 - Learning and Teaching Support Officer.pdf Applications close Sunday, 25 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b4cfca54 Last Name (required) ab6bc8c2 Email (required) 80138ac6 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 30089b62 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Student Services Teaching Support Administration Student Services Teaching Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 93c9bc60 Last Name (required) 05f8b420 Email (required) 200632bd Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
