      "title": "Student Event and Engagement Coordinator (Regional, Remote and Online)",
      "description": "Student Event and Engagement Coordinator (Regional, Remote and Online) - Burnie, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Student Event and Engagement Coordinator (Regional, Remote and Online) 504358 Burnie, TAS Part time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Lead the planning and delivery of student-focused events and initiatives, including Welcome and Orientation, managing communications, budgets, risk mitigation, evaluation and reporting. Supervise Student Engagement Leaders and champion inclusive opportunities that enhance connection, engagement and belonging for diverse student communities. Part time (0.8), Fixed-Term (14 months) position located in Burnie. About the opportunity The Student Events and Engagement Coordinator (Regional, Remote & Online) plays a key role in designing and delivering engaging events, programs and activities that enhance student connection, engagement and belonging throughout the student journey, including Welcome and Orientation and initiatives tailored to regional, remote and online students. The role is responsible for all aspects of event planning and delivery, including communications, budgeting, risk management, evaluation and reporting, and requires some out-of-hours work to support student needs. The position also supervises Student Engagement Leaders, guiding the delivery of events and initiatives that promote inclusion, connection and a strong sense of community across the University. What you’ll do: Work collaboratively with staff throughout the University, TUSA staff and clubs and societies members, to manage, develop and deliver fit for purpose experiences and events for students studying on the Cradle Coast Campuses and online. Manage all aspects of event planning and delivery inclusive of compliance, budgetary and governance requirements. Engage and collaborate with colleagues within an institutional wide team, to deliver events engagement opportunities for students located in North West Tasmania and online. Collate and analyse data to inform future events and activities delivered and for reporting purposes. Participate in other Student Equity and Success projects and programs as required. ­ What we’re looking for: Extensive experience in event management, including, but not limited to - stakeholder engagement, planning, communication, managing providers and risk management. Experience in the design and delivery of online activities or programs that engage diverse groups and follow compliance requirements. Demonstrated experience in supervision or mentoring of junior staff or colleagues. Ability to work effectively and constructively within a team environment. Demonstrated ability to establish rapport and build and maintain relationships across a large and complex organisation. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 6 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $116,872 comprising base salary within the range of $92,120 to $99,891 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact the Pro Vice-Chancellor Student Equity and Success, pvc.student.equity.success@utas.edu.au. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Student Events & Engagement Coordinator (Regional, Remote and Online).pdf . Applications close Sunday, 25 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 2c4e95b4 Last Name (required) 7d3d7d3a Email (required) 6d4c508f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert afb673ae Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Community & Engagement Finance Student Services Administration Community & Engagement Finance Student Services Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Burnie, TAS, Australia Burnie, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 0318af8a Last Name (required) 5ccd8404 Email (required) 81f24fbb Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that 