    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/student-sport-and-partnerships-coordinator-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Student Sport and Partnerships Coordinator",
      "description": "Student Sport and Partnerships Coordinator - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Student Sport and Partnerships Coordinator 504331 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Coordinate a diverse portfolio of student sport programs, competitions and events that promote participation, wellbeing and campus connection. Support the delivery of the Elite Athlete Program, UniSport Nationals, Indigenous Nationals and University Basketball League initiatives. Full-time, ongoing position based in Hobart. About the opportunity As part of the University Sport team, the Student Sport and Partnerships Coordinator supports the development, delivery and coordination of innovative sport and recreation programs that enhance student engagement and contribute to a vibrant campus experience. The role works across a broad range of initiatives including elite athlete support, representative sport, campus recreation activities and affiliated club engagement, while providing operational and administrative support to ensure successful program delivery. What you'll do Collaborate with stakeholders to raise the profile of sport across the University and increase student participation. Coordinate teams competing in the University Basketball League, Indigenous Nationals and UniSport Nationals, including travel and logistical arrangements. Support the delivery of the Elite Athlete Program, providing guidance and support to student athletes. Assist with communications and promotional activities that build awareness and engagement across sporting programs and events. Contribute to the delivery of campus recreation activities, inter-college competitions and community-building initiatives. Provide operational and administrative support to ensure the effective delivery of University sport programs and services. What we're looking for Experience coordinating sport, recreation, wellbeing or community programs and events, or experience in event management. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to engage effectively with a diverse range of students, staff and stakeholders. Strong organisational skills with the ability to manage competing priorities and meet deadlines. Demonstrated commitment to delivering high levels of customer service and stakeholder support. The ability to work both independently and collaboratively within a team environment. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and a 1-2 page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience. You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Mackensie Belbin, Manager Student Sport and Partnerships, Mackensie.Belbin@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description for full details. PD - Student Sport and Partnerships Coordinator.pdf Applications close: Sunday 25th October 2026, 11:55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 86c43697 Last Name (required) e626f5fe Email (required) b9d1ccfe Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 7ef58c58 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Community & Engagement Student Services Community & Engagement Student Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 4ef932c0 Last Name (required) e1ea980d Email (required) 2da93d62 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
