    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/project-officer-hobart-tas-australia-c844d955-c144-4792-97a7-b0b69f84fdf7": {
      "title": "Project Officer",
      "description": "Project Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Project Officer 504363 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 20 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide end-to-end coordination of nationally delivered online training programs, managing student support, stakeholder engagement and program administration. Contribute to the delivery and continuous improvement of critical national education programs, including the Medicines Australia Continuing Education Program and the National Prescribing Curriculum. Full time, Fixed-Term (14 months) position based in Hobart (preferred), Launceston or Burnie. About the opportunity The Project Officer provides high-level administrative and operational support for nationally delivered online training programs, serving as a key contact for students, health professionals, pharmaceutical industry stakeholders and other partners. The role manages student enquiries, course administration, stakeholder guidance, invoicing and payment processes, while working closely with academic and professional staff to support program delivery, continuous improvement and compliance with University, industry and regulatory requirements. As part of the Unit for Medication Outcomes Research and Education (UMORE), the position contributes to nationally significant online education programs, including the mandatory Medicines Australia Continuing Education Program (MA CEP) for prescription pharmaceutical industry employees, and the government-funded National Prescribing Curriculum used by every Australian medical school. What you’ll do: Provide specialist advice and guidance to students, resolving complex enquiries and issues within required timeframes through email, online administration systems and the 1300 helpline, in accordance with relevant policies and procedures. Maintain and develop positive professional relationships with Medicines Australia, pharmaceutical companies and other key stakeholders, acting as a key point of contact for program-related matters. Provide high-level guidance to pharmaceutical companies and employees on the interpretation and application of relevant industry regulatory and training requirements. Contribute to the development and improvement of processes and systems relating to student online study by undertaking continuous reviews and providing recommendations to the team. Manage the end-to-end invoicing and financial administration processes through the University Finance system.  Prepare and analyse monthly financial and revenue reports and provide relevant information and advice to internal and external stakeholders. ­ What we’re looking for: A relevant diploma level qualification with relevant work experience or an equivalent combination of relevant experience and/or education training. Demonstrated effective interpersonal skills, with ability to positively and professionally interact with external partners, staff and students, with experience in negotiating outcomes and success in problem solving and conflict resolution to maintain effective relationships and partnerships. Demonstrated ability to provide high-level professional and confidential guidance on the interpretation and application of relevant regulations, industry requirements and compliance matters, in accordance with privacy and legislative requirements. Demonstrated ability to work both autonomously and as a team member, within established guidelines, and manage competing priorities using discretion, confidentiality, and sound judgement. Highly developed administrative, organisational and problem-solving skills, with a strong attention to detail and demonstrated ability to prioritise competing demands, manage workloads and meet deadlines. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Tristan Ling, Senior Research Fellow, Tristan.Ling@utas.edu.au or 6226 7396 Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position-Description - Project Officer.pdf . Applications close Tuesday, 20 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) cf2402f5 Last Name (required) 2bfee4bd Email (required) 3e289ade Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert fe188ebf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Finance Administration Finance Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 09b60af2 Last Name (required) 2b7d73d6 Email (required) 9a2929ad Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
