    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-in-nursing-hobart-tas-australia-launceston": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer in Nursing",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer in Nursing - Hobart, TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Senior Lecturer in Nursing 504326 Hobart, TAS Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide academic leadership across undergraduate and postgraduate nursing education Lead curriculum innovation, teaching excellence and the development of academic colleagues Full-time or part-time opportunity based in Hobart or Launceston About the opportunity The University of Tasmania is seeking an experienced nursing academic to join the School of Nursing as a Senior Lecturer in Nursing. This is an opportunity to take a leading role in shaping contemporary nursing education, contributing to the quality and development of our undergraduate and postgraduate programs while supporting positive outcomes for students, colleagues and the nursing profession. As Senior Lecturer, you will provide academic leadership across learning and teaching, lead and contribute to curriculum design and review, support quality and accreditation activities, and champion evidence-informed and innovative approaches to nursing education. You will also play an important role in mentoring and developing academic colleagues and supporting high-quality, consistent teaching across the School. Drawing on your contemporary nursing expertise and higher education experience, you will build strong relationships across the University and with health services, the profession and community, helping ensure our programs remain relevant, responsive and connected to contemporary practice. Depending on the successful candidate's experience and workload profile, the role may also include research and scholarship aligned with School and University priorities. This is a great opportunity for an established nursing academic ready to influence educational practice, develop others and contribute to the future direction of nursing education in Tasmania. For candidates considering a move to Tasmania, relocation assistance is available to support the successful candidate. What you’ll do: Provide academic leadership in the delivery of high-quality undergraduate and postgraduate nursing education. Lead and contribute to curriculum design, development and review, assessment quality and academic quality assurance. Drive innovative, evidence-informed approaches to learning and teaching that enhance student engagement, success and the student experience. Lead teaching teams and mentor and support the development of early-career academics and teaching colleagues. Build productive partnerships with health services, professional colleagues, industry and the wider community. Contribute to research and/or scholarly activity appropriate to the successful candidate's workload profile and Academic Level C expectations.­ What we’re looking for: Current registration as a Nurse with the Nursing and Midwifery Board of Australia with no conditions. A PhD qualification (or working towards) in nursing or a closely related health field. For a teaching-intensive appointment, substantial relevant professional and scholarly achievement may be considered in accordance with University requirements. Demonstrated achievement and leadership in university-level learning and teaching, including course coordination, curriculum development and contemporary teaching practice. Significant and recent nursing practice experience, with the ability to translate contemporary clinical knowledge into engaging and relevant learning experiences. A track record of innovation in learning, teaching and curriculum. Strong leadership and organisational capability, including experience developing others and leading collaborative teaching activity. The ability to build effective partnerships across the profession, health sector and wider community. For a balanced academic appointment, an established record of research and scholarship appropriate to Academic Level C. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. Relocation assistance of up to $5,000 is available for the successful candidate. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the Roles Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience. For further information about this position, please contact Associate Professor Farida Saghafi, Interim Head, School of Nursing, Farida.Saghafi@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - 504326 - Senior Lecturer in Nursing.pdf Applications close Sunday, 25 October 2026, 11.55pm Interviews are planned for Friday, 30 October 2026, with shortlisted candidates to be contacted soon after applications close. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) fcaae280 Last Name (required) c6715823 Email (required) 5efe0ca4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 261783fd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 985f5668 Last Name (required) 29c1df6e Email (required) 4f3de918 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
