    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/manager-indigenous-curriculum-quality-and-performance-health-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Manager Indigenous Curriculum Quality and Performance, Health",
      "description": "Manager Indigenous Curriculum Quality and Performance, Health - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Manager Indigenous Curriculum Quality and Performance, Health 504332 Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 1 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites Influence curriculum strategy across Health Academic Units Use data and insights to strengthen student and graduate outcomes Full time, ongoing position based in Burnie, New Norfolk, Hobart or Launceston The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa, Wangal and Gadigal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We pay our respects to Elders past and present who hold memories, knowledges and culture, and their enduring cultural practices of caring for Country that spans millennia. About the Opportunity As the Manager Indigenous Curriculum Quality and Performance, Health, you will provide strategic leadership to support the consistent implementation and ongoing development of Indigenous curriculum across Health. Working closely with the latawina Blak Health Collective and academic leaders, you will help embed the latawina Aboriginal Health Curriculum Framework and strengthen culturally safe education. In addition, you will: Provide strategic advice on curriculum quality, performance, governance, risk and regulatory compliance. Establish and manage Indigenous curriculum audits, performance measures, benchmarking and reporting. Use data and analytics to inform curriculum performance, student success, graduate outcomes and health workforce pathways. Collaborate with Aboriginal Leads, Associate Heads Learning and Teaching Performance and Course Coordinators to support curriculum development and improvement. Establish governance processes for curriculum redesign, aligned with the latawina Cultural Authority Model and University policies, and support professional accreditation requirements. Contribute to strategic and operational planning for the ongoing Indigenisation of curricula across Health. Support the development and implementation of latawina Graduate Cultural Capability resources, cultural safety and anti-racism learning modules. About the University At the University of Tasmania, we have a mission to make a difference for Tasmania, and from Tasmania. With our unique location and history, we have both an obligation and opportunity to make a global contribution. People are at the heart of that contribution. We focus on building a workplace culture where we come together in a way that empowers us all to connect, belong and grow. The University is one of the largest employers in our State, with main campuses in three distinct regions: Nipaluna/Hobart, Launceston, and Pataway/Burnie. We also have a specialised health campus in Sydney. We strive to stimulate economic growth, lift literacy, improve health outcomes for Tasmania and nurture our environment as it nurtures us. We welcome enquiring minds, from near and far, to join us in our pursuit of the extraordinary. What’s Required Strong knowledge and experience of Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander community, culture, and ways of knowing and being, particularly as they relate to Indigenous health and health leadership. Extensive experience in tertiary learning and teaching quality assurance, governance and curriculum development. Demonstrated experience in Indigenous curriculum mapping, implementation and review. Strong data analytics and reporting capability, with the ability to use insights to inform performance and improvement. Highly developed interpersonal and communication skills, with the ability to build trusted relationships across disciplines and teams. Demonstrated experience collaborating across Academic Units and institutional teams to achieve shared outcomes. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and in a culturally informed and sensitive manner with Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander People. The ability to provide strategic advice and translate strategy into practical action. A postgraduate qualification in Indigenous Education, or an equivalent combination of qualifications and relevant experience. This is an Identified Position. You must be an Aboriginal and/or Torres Strait Islander person to be considered for this opportunity. Candidates must provide eligibility documentation with their application. Please contact aboriginal.employment@utas.edu.au to discuss the documentation required. What’s on Offer? On offer is a full time, ongoing opportunity based in Lutruwita/Tasmania (with a preference for Walawali/New Norfolk or Pataway/Burnie) with a competitive remuneration package. We value our staff and the important contributions they make to our community. You’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 5 days Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Cultural leave annually 17% superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and car hire discounts Health insurance and banking Novated Leasing Belong - Be You People are at the heart of everything we do. Our vision is to ensure that our people feel encouraged and supported to bring their whole selves to work. Fostering diversity and inclusion is our key priority, supporting our communities to come together in ways that empower connection, learning, belonging and growth. Celebrating the strengths that diversity brings will enable us to achieve our vision and mission. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community. Tell us how we can make this job work for you. Remuneration Appointment to this role will be at HEO Level 9 and will have a remuneration package of up to $160,613, comprising of a base salary within the range of $130,242 to $137,276 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume And a cover letter outlining your motivation for the role and full responses to the success criteria outlined in the Position Description For further information about this position, please contact Professor Adele Holloway, Dean Learning and Teaching Performance - Health at a.f.holloway@utas.edu.au , Professor Jen Evans, Aboriginal Health Leadership at Jen.Evans@utas.edu.au , or aboriginal.employment@utas.edu.au . Applications close 11:55pm Sunday 1st of November 2026 Manager Indigenous Curiculum and Quality Position Description.pdf As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 449f3c28 Last Name (required) bfe6243d Email (required) 4ca41adf Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6a77dbe0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Administration Management Student Services Administration Management Student Services Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia First Name (required) 4d584a96 Last Name (required) 0332843c Email (required) d684f2b8 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candi