    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-health-sociology-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia-launceston": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Health Sociology",
      "description": "Lecturer in Health Sociology - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer in Health Sociology 504314 Launceston, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 28 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Teach Health Sociology across undergraduate and postgraduate programs Embed cultural safety and Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander perspectives in health education Full time, ongoing position based in Launceston About the Opportunity As a Lecturer in Health Sociology you will work within a collaborative, multi-disciplinary team to deliver programs and teach students attending University of Tasmania campuses located in Launceston, Hobart, Burnie, and Sydney. This position is a teaching-intensive academic role with a particular focus on embedding cultural safety into the learning content within our contributions to the University’s nursing and allied health curriculum. The position will require success in teaching, research and service, with a research allocation designed to contribute to the School’s record of research excellence and impact in health sociology. About the University At the University of Tasmania, we have a mission to make a difference for Tasmania, and from Tasmania. With our unique location and history, we have both an obligation and opportunity to make a global contribution. People are at the heart of that contribution. We focus on building a workplace culture where we come together in a way that empowers us all to connect, belong and grow. The University is one of the largest employers in our State, with campuses in three distinct regions: Hobart, Launceston, and Burnie. We also have a specialised health campus in Sydney. We strive to stimulate economic growth, lift literacy, improve health outcomes for Tasmania and nurture our environment as it nurtures us. We welcome enquiring minds, from near and far, to join us in our pursuit of the extraordinary . What’s Required A PhD or equivalent in a relevant social science field. A demonstrated record of, and continuing commitment to, research in the field of health sociology. Experience in University-level teaching and learning across different delivery modes, including online and face-to-face. Teaching and/or research experience in cultural safety. Excellent written and verbal communication skills with the ability to relate effectively and thoughtfully to students and staff from a variety of backgrounds and cultures. A proven ability to work effectively independently and as part of discipline-based and multi-disciplinary teams. What’s on Offer? On offer is a full time, ongoing opportunity based in Launceston with a competitive remuneration package. We value our staff and the important contributions they make to our community. You’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 5 days Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Cultural leave annually 17% superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and car hire discounts Health insurance and banking Novated Leasing Relocation support available for those considering a move to Tasmania Belong – Be You People are at the heart of everything we do. Our vision is to ensure that our people feel encouraged and supported to bring their whole selves to work. Fostering diversity and inclusion is our key priority, supporting our communities to come together in ways that empower connection, learning, belonging and growth. Celebrating the strengths that diversity brings will enable us to achieve our vision and mission. Applications are encouraged from all sectors of the community. Tell us how we can make this job work for you. Remuneration Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B and will have a remuneration package of up to $155,885 comprising of a base salary within the range of $114,766 to $133,235 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume A 1–2-page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role A statement addressing the selection criteria by outlining how your skills and experience align with the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description For further information about this position, please contact Professor Vaughan Higgins, Professor, Sociology at vaughan.higgins@utas.edu.au Associate Professor Peta Cook, Associate Professor in Sociology at peta.cook@utas.edu.au Applications close 11:55pm Wednesday 28th of October 2026 Lecturer in Health Sociology - Position Description (504314).pdf We are also recruiting for a Lecturer/Senior Lecturer in Health Sociology (Indigenous).  Take a look at our other role and explore which opportunity is the right fit for you. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 981a37f5 Last Name (required) ab0e5dae Email (required) 041f8134 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 14270200 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Intensive Teaching Intensive Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia First Name (required) 9e22dc13 Last Name (required) 45c807fe Email (required) 88943331 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
