    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/dean-and-head-of-school-law-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Dean and Head of School, Law",
      "description": "Dean and Head of School, Law - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Dean and Head of School, Law 503597 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 30 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Shape the future of legal education and student success Strengthen research excellence and external partnerships Lead academic strategy, people, performance, and culture About the Opportunity The School of Law at the University of Tasmania is one of Australia’s oldest and most respected centres of legal education, with a proud history dating back to 1893. This is an exceptional opportunity for an accomplished academic leader to shape the future of a distinguished law school that is committed to excellence in legal education, impactful research, and meaningful engagement with the legal profession and wider community. As Dean and Head of School, you will provide strategic, academic, and operational leadership, fostering a culture of collaboration, innovation, and high performance. You will lead the School’s contribution to the University’s strategic goals, strengthen partnerships across government, industry and the legal sector, and support the development of graduates equipped to make a positive impact in Tasmania, Australia and beyond. This role offers the opportunity to build on a strong legacy while guiding the School into its next chapter of growth and influence. About the University The University of Tasmania is a mission-driven institution dedicated to making a difference for Lutruwita/Tasmania and a distinctive contribution from Tasmania to the world. As the sole university on the island, the University is deeply embedded in the social, economic, and environmental fabric of Tasmania, working in close partnership with communities, industry, and government to address key challenges in education, health, productivity, and climate action. The University takes pride in its place-based identity, leveraging Tasmania’s unique geography, culture, and resources to offer world-leading research and education. What We are Looking For We are seeking an outstanding academic leader with a strong track record of achievement in legal education, research, and engagement. You will bring the vision to shape the future of legal education, the leadership capability to foster a high-performing and collaborative culture, and the strategic insight to navigate a rapidly evolving higher education environment. With experience leading academic excellence, research growth, and operational performance, you will be skilled at building meaningful partnerships across the legal profession, government, industry, and the community. A deep understanding of the opportunities and challenges facing legal education, together with a commitment to innovation, student success, and institutional impact, will position you to lead the School's next chapter with confidence and ambition. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume and: A 1-page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role at the University of Tasmania A separate response of up to 3-pages related to the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description For further information about this position, please contact the Talent Acquisition team via email: TalentTeam@utas.edu.au Applications Close Friday the 30th of October at 11.55pm 2026 Position Description - Dean and Head of School Law - September 2026.pdf To be eligible for this position, you are required to have Australian citizenship, permanent residence or a current valid visa that allows you to fulfill the requirements of this role. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police background checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) e7ce287a Last Name (required) 6a58f8ee Email (required) f9a16516 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 876329ba Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Management Management Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 9b99635b Last Name (required) 7cb0cb63 Email (required) b7daf251 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
