    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/head-school-of-health-sciences-launceston-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Head, School of Health Sciences",
      "description": "Head, School of Health Sciences - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Head, School of Health Sciences 503787 Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 25 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Build impactful partnerships across health services, government, industry and communities to shape Tasmania's future health workforce. Lead a diverse portfolio spanning allied health, exercise and sports science, and laboratory medicine. Foster a high-performing, inclusive and collaborative culture. About the Opportunity We are seeking to appoint an exceptional and inspiring leader as Head of School, Health Sciences, based in Launceston, Tasmania. This is a rare opportunity to lead a School that is making a tangible difference to the health and wellbeing of Tasmanian communities through education, research and partnership. Home to disciplines spanning allied health, exercise and sports science, and laboratory medicine, the School is uniquely positioned at the intersection of community need, workforce development and health innovation. Based within the University's state-of-the-art facilities in Launceston, you will lead a collaborative and interdisciplinary academic community united by a shared purpose: improving lives through better health outcomes. Through deep partnerships with health services, government, industry and community organisations, the School is shaping the next generation of health professionals and helping address Tasmania's most pressing workforce and health challenges. As a key member of the UTAS Health leadership team, you will help realise the University's vision of creating healthier, more connected communities. This is an opportunity to influence the future of Tasmania's health system through education, research and collaboration, strengthening workforce capability and delivering lasting impact for generations to come. About the University The University of Tasmania is a mission-driven institution dedicated to making a difference for Lutruwita/Tasmania and a distinctive contribution from Tasmania to the world. As the sole university on the island, the University is deeply embedded in the social, economic, and environmental fabric of Tasmania, working in close partnership with communities, industry, and government to address key challenges in education, health, productivity, and climate action. The University takes pride in its place-based identity, leveraging Tasmania’s unique geography, culture, and resources to offer world-leading research and education. What We are Looking For We are seeking an accomplished and collaborative leader who is passionate about the role higher education can play in improving health outcomes and building workforce capability. You will bring significant leadership experience within a university, health or allied health setting, along with the ability to inspire high-performing teams and foster a mission-driven culture of excellence, inclusion and innovation. With a strong understanding of the contemporary health landscape, you will be skilled at building strategic partnerships, navigating complexity and balancing academic, operational and financial priorities. Most importantly, you will be a values-led leader who thinks beyond organisational boundaries, embraces collaboration, and is motivated by the opportunity to make a lasting contribution to Tasmania's communities, health system and future workforce. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Generous relocation support to Tasmania How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume and: A 1-2 page cover letter outlining your motivation for the role at the University of Tasmania A separate response outlining how your skills and experience align with the role specific skills, knowledge and experience in the Position Description Applications close 11.55pm Sunday the 25th of October 2026. Position Description Head of Health Sciences Sept 2026 .pdf For further information about this position, please contact the Talent Acquisition team via email: TalentTeam@utas.edu.au To be eligible for this position, you are required to have Australian citizenship, permanent residence or a current valid visa that allows you to fulfill the requirements of this role. As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police background checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 59698e81 Last Name (required) 9854ca4e Email (required) fdcd410b Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b33a9ec0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Balanced Research/Teaching Balanced Research/Teaching Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) d76014dd Last Name (required) cbdde2c0 Email (required) 613ae3a6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
