    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/research-fellow-digital-forests-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia-hobart": {
      "title": "Research Fellow Digital Forests",
      "description": "Research Fellow Digital Forests - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Research Fellow Digital Forests 504144 Hobart, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 18 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. · Drive innovation in digital forestry and geospatial analytics · Work with industry to translate research into operational outcomes · Relocation support may be available for suitable candidates moving to Tasmania About the Opportunity We are seeking to appoint a Senior Research Fellow or Principal Research Fellow, Digital Forests to join the Australian Forest and Wood Innovations (AFWI) Centre for Sustainable Resource and Product Solutions. This fixed-term appointment offers a unique opportunity to shape the future of digital forest monitoring and inventory across Australia. Over the next four years, you will help bridge the gap between emerging sensing technologies and their practical application in forest management, planning and reporting. Working at the intersection of research, technology and industry, you will lead the development of innovative approaches using multi-sensor lidar, imaging analytics and geospatial data to improve forest inventory, monitoring and decision-making. We welcome applications from candidates with experience across academia, industry, consulting or government. Whether your expertise has been developed through applied research, operational forestry, environmental consulting or public sector leadership, this role offers the opportunity to deliver nationally significant impact through collaboration, innovation and real-world application. About the University The University of Tasmania is a mission-driven institution dedicated to making a difference for Lutruwita/Tasmania and a distinctive contribution from Tasmania to the world. As the sole university on the island, the University is deeply embedded in the social, economic, and environmental fabric of Tasmania, working in close partnership with communities, industry, and government to address key challenges in education, health, productivity, and climate action. The University takes pride in its place-based identity, leveraging Tasmania’s unique geography, culture, and resources to offer world-leading research and education. What We are Looking For We welcome applications from individuals with deep expertise in digital forestry, remote sensing, geospatial analytics, environmental data science or related disciplines. While a PhD is valued, we recognise that expertise can be developed through a variety of career pathways. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose experience has been built in industry, consulting, government agencies or applied research environments. The successful candidate will bring a strong track record of translating technical innovation into practical outcomes and working collaboratively with stakeholders to address real-world challenges in forest inventory, monitoring and management. You will have demonstrated leadership experience, including leading projects and teams, building productive partnerships, mentoring others, securing funding or commercial work, and delivering outcomes across complex organisational environments. We are seeking a leader who can bridge the gap between emerging technologies and industry adoption, engaging confidently with both technical specialists and operational decision-makers. The role may be appointed at either Senior Research Fellow or Principal Research Fellow level. Please refer to the relevant Position Description for the full role requirements, including the qualifications, skills, experience and leadership capabilities sought at each level. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world, and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. In return for your experience, you’ll have access to an array of staff benefits and discounts including: · 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers · 17% Superannuation contribution · Health and fitness membership options · Accommodation and Car Hire discounts · Health Insurance and Banking · Novated Leasing · Relocation Support Salary Details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C or D and will have a total remuneration package of up to $210,621 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $180,018 plus 17% superannuation. Relocation support may be available to the successful candidate, helping make a move to Tasmania as seamless as possible. How to Apply? If this role is of interest, we look forward to hearing from you. Please provide your up-to-date resume and: · A cover letter (maximum two pages) outlining your interest in the role and how your skills, knowledge and experience align with the role-specific requirements detailed in the Position Description. · Applications close 11.55pm Sunday the 18 of October. · For general enquiries about the recruitment process, the University, relocation support, or employment opportunities at the University of Tasmania, please contact the Talent Acquisition Team at TalentTeam@utas.edu.au . · For role-specific enquiries, please contact Arko Lucieer, Head of School, Geography, Planning and Spatial Sciences, via email at arko.lucieer@utas.edu.au . Position Description-Level-C AFWI DigitalForests .pdf Position Description-Level D AFWI DigitalForests.pdf As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police background checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a66ef8cc Last Name (required) 4a93f200 Email (required) aa4b8920 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Teaching Laboratory Technician Hobart, TAS Laboratory & Research Support Play a key role in supporting hands-on teaching and learning, helping to deliver safe, engaging and well-organised laboratory experiences for our students Sign up for job alerts Job Alert c81d6d9c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Research Intensive Research Intensive Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia First Name (required) d23621f7 Last Name (required) 945ca408 Email (required) aa77a757 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
