    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/client-services-officer-hobart-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Client Services Officer",
      "description": "Client Services Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Client Services Officer 504330 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 29 Oct 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide online, face-to-face, and remote IT support, troubleshooting technical issues and delivering timely, effective solutions for end users. Create and maintain user documentation while providing expert guidance on ICT services, ensuring a high level of customer satisfaction and service excellence. Full time, Fixed-Term (12 months) position located in Hobart. About the opportunity The Client Services Officer, IT Services provides high-quality customer service and responsive IT support across a broad range of ICT services at the University of Tasmania. The role delivers online, face-to-face, and remote technical support, troubleshooting and resolving IT issues, providing guidance to end users, and creating and maintaining user documentation. Operating to agreed service levels, the position focuses on the efficient delivery of support services, clear communication, timely resolution of requests and incidents, and achieving high levels of customer satisfaction. What you’ll do: Provide timely and effective IT support via face-to-face, online and remote support, ensuring high levels of customer satisfaction. Develop, update, and maintain comprehensive instruction guides and documentation for end-users. Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues efficiently, escalating complex problems to higher-level support when necessary. Monitor and adhere to agreed service levels, ensuring consistent and reliable IT service delivery. Contribute to continuous improvement initiatives by identifying and suggesting enhancements to IT support processes and services. What we’re looking for: Demonstrated experience with ITIL (Information Technology Infrastructure Library) and/or ITSM (IT Service Management) frameworks. Proven experience in delivering high-quality customer service in an IT support environment. Strong understanding of ICT systems, software, and hardware, with the ability to troubleshoot and resolve technical issues. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to convey technical information clearly and effectively. Strong analytical skills and the ability to think critically to solve complex problems Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Nicholas Brinsmead, Team Leader, Service Delivery, Nicholas.Brinsmead@utas.edu.au or 6226 2730. Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Client Services Officer.pdf . Applications close Thursday, 29 October 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 0ce8310d Last Name (required) 12cfb120 Email (required) ea0e19ab Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Officer Hobart, TAS Administration, Laboratory & Research Support Make a meaningful impact on health research by supporting innovative studies that help improve outcomes for people affected by Bone Marrow Failure. Learning Adviser (STEM/Numeracy) Hobart, TAS Student Services, Teaching Support Deliver specialist learning development support in STEM-related areas, including numeracy, mathematics, statistics, quantitative reasoning, scientific literacy and data interpretation. Lecturer in English Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of English education and inspire the next generation of readers, writers and critical thinkers through innovative and engaging learning experiences Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 48051e5a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Information Technology Information Technology Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Hobart, TAS, Australia Hobart, TAS, Australia First Name (required) 60846453 Last Name (required) 352595ba Email (required) 3a133ede Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
