    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/senior-lecturer-psychology-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia-hobart": {
      "title": "Senior Lecturer Psychology",
      "description": "Senior Lecturer Psychology - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Senior Lecturer Psychology 504456 Hobart, TAS Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Full time Closing on: 15 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the palawa/pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Provide academic leadership in psychology education and professional training. Teach and supervise students across undergraduate and postgraduate programs. Contribute to impactful research and strengthen psychology workforce outcomes for Tasmania and beyond. Full time, Academic Level C opportunity based in Tasmania. About the Opportunity The University of Tasmania is seeking an experienced and collaborative psychologist to join the School of Psychological Sciences as a Senior Lecturer. Working within a student-centred academic environment, you will play an important role in preparing future psychologists through outstanding teaching, placement supervision, curriculum development and professional practice education. You will work closely with academic colleagues, professional staff and industry partners to ensure our programs continue to meet contemporary professional and accreditation standards while responding to workforce and mental health needs across Tasmania and beyond. This role offers an opportunity to contribute to a university committed to making a difference for Tasmania while helping shape the future of psychology education, clinical training and research. What you’ll do Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University's strategic objectives and academic mission. Deliver high-quality teaching across undergraduate and postgraduate psychology programs. Provide supervision and support for students undertaking professional practice placements. Contribute to curriculum development and continuous improvement aligned with accreditation requirements. Undertake high-quality research and scholarly activity. Supervise higher degree research students. Build and maintain productive partnerships with the psychology profession, health services and community stakeholders. Contribute to a collaborative and inclusive academic culture. What we’re looking for A PhD or equivalent in Psychology. Current registration as a psychologist with AHPRA with no reprimands, undertakings or conditions. Hold a current Working with Vulnerable People (WWVP). Psychology Board of Australia Approved Supervisor status. Demonstrated success in university-level teaching and learning. Knowledge of Australian Psychology Accreditation Council (APAC) accreditation standards and their application in curriculum design. A strong research track record, including publications and scholarly contributions. Experience supervising provisionally registered psychologists. Clinical experience relevant to the position. A demonstrated ability to build effective relationships across the profession, industry and community. What’s on Offer? As we look toward 2050, we remain committed to fostering excellence, collaboration, and transformative education - preparing graduates to navigate the challenges of a rapidly changing world and shape its future. While remaining true to our Tasmanian roots, this career defining role will see you significantly contribute to our dedication to making a difference for, and from, Tasmania. You’ll have access an array of staff benefits and discounts including. 26 Weeks paid parental leave for primary care givers 17% Superannuation contribution Health and fitness membership options Accommodation and Car Hire discounts Health Insurance and Banking Novated Leasing Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level C and will have a total remuneration package of up to $184,076 comprising base salary within the range of $138,536 to $157,330 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply? To apply online, please provide the following supporting documentation: Resume Cover letter outlining your suitability and motivation for the role Your responses to the success criteria from the Position Description below For further information about this position, please contact Kimberley Norris, Head of School, School of Psychological Sciences Kimberley.Norris@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Senior Lecturer Psychology.pdf Applications close Sunday 15 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Recommended Jobs AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. Technical Officer Launceston, TAS Infrastructure & Property, Teaching Support Firefighter, defence, maintenance or trade background? Put your practical skills to work at the Australian Maritime College's Emergency Response Centre and help train the next generation of maritime professionals Cultural Collections Officer (Tyler Collection) Hobart, TAS Library Support the ethical care, display and activation of collections, bringing the Tyler Collection of Romanian and Modern Art to life for teaching, research and public engagement. © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/technical-officer-launceston-tas-australia-723276ad-dfe6-4683-b883-985a3a709662": {
      "title": "Technical Officer",
      "description": "Technical Officer - Launceston, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Technical Officer 504364 Launceston, TAS Full time Closing on: 10 Nov 2026 Add to favourites View favourites The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Hands-on role maintaining specialist emergency response training facilities and equipment Join Australia's leading maritime education provider at Bell Bay, enjoy great employee benefits and 17% superannuation Full time Monday to Friday, ongoing role based in Bell Bay About the opportunity Join the Australian Maritime College's Emergency Response Centre at Bell Bay and play a hands-on role maintaining specialist training facilities, equipment and emergency response infrastructure used by students, industry and researchers. The Australian Maritime College (AMC), a specialist institute of the University of Tasmania, is recognised globally for excellence in maritime education, training and research. Our National Centre for Seafaring and Maritime Operations delivers industry-leading training and operates world-class facilities, including advanced simulation centres, specialist laboratories and maritime training infrastructure. We are seeking a practical, safety-focused, hands-on Technical Officer to support the operation of our Bell Bay Emergency Response Centre. You'll help maintain specialist emergency response training facilities, equipment and infrastructure, ensuring students receive an exceptional training experience in a safe and realistic environment. No two days are the same. From preparing fire and emergency response training equipment to coordinating maintenance activities, conducting safety inspections and supervising contractors, you'll play a key role in keeping the facility operating at its best. What you’ll do: Ensure a high focus on safety, wellbeing and risk management across a broad range of activities and processes. Undertake and coordinate routine planned and reactive maintenance activities and repairs of plant and equipment and facilities to ensure the highest level of quality operation and student training outcomes. Prepare training and practical equipment in connection with fire and emergency response activities. Engage with and supervise contractors from various trades to ensure that work is undertaken in a safe and timely manner whilst achieving positive outcomes. Undertake and maintain high standards of risk management, including risk assessments, SOPs, WHS inspections and audits of facilities, plant and equipment. Maintain accurate documentation and initiate corrective action requests to ensure compliance with relevant legislation and industry standards.­ What we’re looking for: We value practical experience as much as formal qualifications and encourage applications from individuals with backgrounds in emergency services, defence, maritime operations, industrial maintenance, trades or other operational environments. Demonstrated ability to coordinate multiple operational activities and manage competing priorities. Strong problem-solving skills and attention to detail. Experience supervising contractors or leading activities within a technical or training environment. A commitment to workplace health, safety and risk management. Sound digital literacy skills, including the ability to use Microsoft Office applications and maintain accurate electronic records. Desirable Qualifications and Licences: Current driver licence National High-Risk Work Licence (Forklift Truck) Working at Heights Certificate Confined Space Certificate First Aid/CPR Certification Current Working with Vulnerable People registration or the ability to obtain Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 5 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $105,665 comprising a base salary within the range of $80,869 to $90,312 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the success profile. For further information about this position, please contact Geoff Eyers, Marine Manager, Geoff.Eyers@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Technical Officer - 504364.pdf Applications close Tuesday, 10 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 1e30ab3b Last Name (required) e31ca756 Email (required) 9c43951f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. Senior Lecturer Psychology Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of psychology education and clinical training in Tasmania. Join the University of Tasmania's School of Psychological Sciences and contribute to high-quality teaching, supervision, research and professional engagement that supports the next generation of psychologists. Cultural Collections Officer (Tyler Collection) Hobart, TAS Library Support the ethical care, display and activation of collections, bringing the Tyler Collection of Romanian and Modern Art to life for teaching, research and public engagement. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 56d4f716 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Infrastructure & Property Teaching Support Infrastructure & Property Teaching Support Employment Type Full time Full time Locations Launceston, TAS, Australia Launceston, TAS, Australia First Name (required) e2bf62fd Last Name (required) 744ce895 Email (required) 6a3fd210 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
