    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/event-support-officer-hobart-tas-australia-c8860a1d-ff2f-45e4-9b92-98e7dad3f83a": {
      "title": "Event Support Officer",
      "description": "Event Support Officer - Hobart, TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:00 Loaded : 0% Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 0:00 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Event Support Officer 504250 Hobart, TAS Full time Closing on: 4 Nov 2026 Are you an organised multitasker with a passion for events and providing exceptional experiences? Assist with the setup, pack-down, and on-site delivery of university events across Tasmania Full time, Fixed Term (until September 2027) based in Hobart The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. About the opportunity The University of Tasmania's Brand Team is looking for a Hobart-based Event Support Officer to fill a vacancy created through internal career progression. The Event Support Officer is responsible for supporting the delivery of key University of Tasmania events and activations, including Open Days, Graduations, School Leaver Expos, and student engagement initiatives. Combining event logistics, equipment and inventory management, and on-the-ground operational support, this role is central to ensuring events run smoothly and successfully. As part of the Brand Team, you will work collaboratively with colleagues and stakeholders to deliver memorable experiences that showcase the University and strengthen engagement with students, schools, and the wider community. This role requires flexibility to travel between university campuses, event venues, and interstate (as required), as well as the ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as part of a rostered schedule. The successful candidate will be comfortable undertaking manual handling and lifting tasks and be capable of safely operating a small electric utility vehicle on campus. What you’ll do: Assist with the setup, pack-down, and on-site delivery of university events across Tasmania. Maintain and organise event storerooms, including inventory tracking of equipment, signage, and merchandise. Assist with the coordination and logistics of merchandise pop-up shops and online store fulfilment. Provide general administrative support for event planning and delivery, including completing documentation such as risk assessments and checklists. Assist with event-related logistics and coordination tasks, including online ticketing, scheduling, travel arrangements, and basic invoice processing. Undertake a range of administrative and operational tasks to support the efficient planning and delivery of University events. ­ What we’re looking for: Ability to safely undertake manual handling tasks and set up, operate, and pack down event equipment, including media walls and related infrastructure. Demonstrated experience coordinating event logistics, including scheduling, resource allocation, supplier coordination, and on-site event delivery. Ability to operate, troubleshoot, and support basic audiovisual (AV) equipment and event infrastructure, with experience using event management systems. Sound understanding of risk management and Work Health and Safety (WHS) requirements, including the preparation of risk assessments, safety checklists, and other compliance documentation. Experience managing storeroom operations, including inventory tracking, stock control, and maintaining accurate records. Strong interpersonal and stakeholder engagement skills, with the ability to build effective relationships with staff, suppliers, contractors, and service providers. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and the ability to quickly learn and use organisational systems for finance, scheduling, and stakeholder engagement. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at HEO 4 and will have a total remuneration package of up to $91,488 comprising base salary within the range of $73,814 to $78,195 plus 17% superannuation. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience. You do not need to separately address the success profile. • For further information about this position, please contact Elena Arena, Brand Events Manager at Elena.Arena@utas.edu.au . Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description below for full details. Position Description - 504250 - Event Support Officer.pdf Applications close Wednesday, 4 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Recommended Jobs AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. Senior Lecturer Psychology Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of psychology education and clinical training in Tasmania. Join the University of Tasmania's School of Psychological Sciences and contribute to high-quality teaching, supervision, research and professional engagement that supports the next generation of psychologists. Technical Officer Launceston, TAS Infrastructure & Property, Teaching Support Firefighter, defence, maintenance or trade background? Put your practical skills to work at the Australian Maritime College's Emergency Response Centre and help train the next generation of maritime professionals © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
