    "https://careers.utas.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-therapeutics-and-pharmacy-practice-statewide-all-locations-in-tasmania-tas-australia": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice",
      "description": "Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice - Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Skip to main content Visit UTAS My Profile Kiosk mode Jobs and Careers Looking to become part of a welcoming and collaborative community making a difference for Tasmania and the World? View our current career opportunities here. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:26 Loaded : 0% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:26 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice 504384 Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Part time Closing on: 8 Nov 2026 The University of Tasmania acknowledges the Palawa/Pakana and Gadigal/Wangal people as the traditional custodians of the land, sea and waters of the areas upon which we live and work. We recognise their valuable contributions and deep connection to country and pay respect to Elders past and present. Inspire and educate the next generation of pharmacists through contemporary, clinically focused teaching Build your academic and research profile within a supportive and collaborative health sciences environment Part-time (0.8 FTE), ongoing role based in Hobart, offering flexibility, excellent employee benefits and relocation support for the preferred candidate About the opportunity Whether you're an established academic or an experienced pharmacist considering a transition into higher education, this is an opportunity to make a lasting impact on the profession. Join the University of Tasmania as a Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice and help educate the next generation of pharmacists while contributing to research that improves health outcomes locally and globally. This position involves teaching and coordinating a range of units encompassing therapeutics and pharmacy practice primarily within the Bachelor of Pharmacy with Honours program. The ideal candidate will embrace contemporary teaching techniques and technology to enhance both online and face-to-face education, particularly in clinical contexts. Based in Hobart, this role offers the opportunity to build your academic profile within a collaborative and supportive environment while enjoying the professional and lifestyle benefits of living and working in Tasmania. What you’ll do – Key Outcomes: Make an effective and sustained contribution to the University in achieving its strategic objectives and fulfilling its operational responsibilities. Provide high-quality contemporary online and face-to-face teaching in undergraduate and postgraduate courses with a commitment to continual improvement in the quality of teaching and the student experience. Demonstrate a scholarly approach to teaching and curriculum development, aligning with the University’s quality framework and delivery standards. Undertake and contribute to high-quality research and scholarly activity in therapeutics, pharmacy practice, health professions education or a related field. Contribute to the development and maintenance of productive and effective links inside the University and locally and nationally with the discipline, relevant interdisciplinary domains, profession, industry and/or wider community. ­ Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience Pharmacy practice professional experience, ideally in a range of clinical settings. Clinical expertise with contemporary therapeutic knowledge and an ability to contribute to discipline research in the field of therapeutics and pharmacy practice. Demonstrated experience in, or capacity to contribute to, high-quality University-level learning and teaching in online, clinical and face-to-face environments. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within a team to achieve a common goal and in a manner that aligns with the University’s values. A record of contributing to building and maintaining effective and productive links locally and nationally with the discipline, profession, industry (where relevant) and wider community. Qualifications and Licences A PhD or equivalent in a relevant field is desirable. Applicants without a PhD may be considered where they demonstrate substantial relevant professional, clinical or educational experience. Current registration as a Pharmacist with the Pharmacy Board of Australia. Exceptions may be made for individuals who are eligible for registration. Current Registration to Work with Vulnerable People (or to be obtained). Current ‘C’ class driver’s licence or manual vehicle licence Occasional intrastate travel between campuses as required to deliver teaching and learning outcomes. Salary details Appointment to this role will be at Academic Level B and will have a total remuneration package of up to $155,885 pro-rata comprising base salary within the range of $114,766 pro-rata to $133,235 pro-rata plus 17% superannuation. Relocation support may be provided for the preferred candidate. How to Apply To apply online, please provide your CV and 1-2-page cover letter outlining your interest in the role, skills, capabilities and experience.  You do not need to separately address the Role Specific Skills, Knowledge and Experience. For further information about this position, please contact Doctor Daniel Hoyle, Senior Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice, Daniel.Hoyle@utas.edu.au Please visit https://www.utas.edu.au/jobs/applying for our guide to applying and details on the recruitment process. For current UTAS staff, in submitting your application, you acknowledge you have/intend to discuss your interest in this vacancy with your current manager and understand they may need to be contacted confidentially by the hiring manager as part of the assessment of your application. Please refer to the attached Position Description Below for full details. Position Description - Lecturer in Therapeutics and Pharmacy Practice (504384).pdf Applications close Sunday, 8 November 2026, 11.55pm As part of our commitment to a safe and inclusive workplace, employment history and police checks may be conducted as part of the selection process. To be eligible for this position, you are required to hold Australian or New Zealand Citizenship, permanent residency or a valid visa that enables you to fulfil the requirements of this role. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) a883b603 Last Name (required) b919044f Email (required) 2712b15e Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs AFWI Research Contracts Manager Hobart, TAS. Launceston, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Laboratory & Research Support, Legal & Compliance, Management Support nationally significant research by leading contract management and governance across AFWI's research portfolio. Senior Lecturer Psychology Hobart, TAS. Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS Teaching Intensive Shape the future of psychology education and clinical training in Tasmania. Join the University of Tasmania's School of Psychological Sciences and contribute to high-quality teaching, supervision, research and professional engagement that supports the next generation of psychologists. Technical Officer Launceston, TAS Infrastructure & Property, Teaching Support Firefighter, defence, maintenance or trade background? Put your practical skills to work at the Australian Maritime College's Emergency Response Centre and help train the next generation of maritime professionals Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 444d1f31 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Teaching Focused Teaching Focused Employment Type Part time Part time Locations Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia Statewide (all locations in Tasmania), TAS, Australia First Name (required) b7012c62 Last Name (required) b0b25a4d Email (required) b307ee07 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you © 2026  University of Tasmania, Australia. ABN 30 764 374 782. CRICOS Provider Code 00586B Cookie Preferences Copyright Statement Disclaimer Privacy Web accessibility Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
